# Pull Request Checklist

## Before Creating a PR

Use this checklist to ensure your code meets all requirements before submitting a pull request.

## ✅ Code Quality

### General
- [ ] No hardcoded values (strings, dimensions, colors)
- [ ] All strings in `strings.xml`
- [ ] All dimensions use `ResponsiveUtils`
- [ ] All colors use Material Theme
- [ ] Code follows Kotlin coding conventions
- [ ] No unused imports
- [ ] No compiler warnings
- [ ] No lint errors
- [ ] Code is properly formatted

### Architecture
- [ ] Clean Architecture layers respected (Domain ← Data → Presentation)
- [ ] MVVM pattern followed
- [ ] Dependency injection used (Hilt)
- [ ] No direct instantiation of dependencies
- [ ] Repository pattern implemented correctly
- [ ] Use cases contain only business logic
- [ ] ViewModels don't contain UI logic

### State Management
- [ ] State defined in ViewModel
- [ ] State is immutable (StateFlow)
- [ ] State updates use `copy()` or `update()`
- [ ] No mutable state exposed publicly
- [ ] Side effects handled properly (LaunchedEffect, etc.)

### Responsive Design
- [ ] Window size detection implemented
- [ ] Responsive utilities used for all dimensions
- [ ] Layouts adapt to screen sizes (Compact, Medium, Expanded)
- [ ] Navigation adapts to screen size
- [ ] Preview functions for all screen sizes created
- [ ] Tested on multiple screen sizes
- [ ] Landscape orientation tested

## ✅ Testing

### Unit Tests
- [ ] **All ViewModels have unit tests** (≥90% coverage)
- [ ] **All Use Cases have unit tests** (100% coverage)
- [ ] **All Repositories have unit tests** (≥85% coverage)
- [ ] **All Utilities have unit tests** (100% coverage)
- [ ] All tests pass locally
- [ ] Test names are descriptive
- [ ] Tests cover happy paths
- [ ] Tests cover error scenarios
- [ ] Tests cover edge cases
- [ ] Tests use MockK for mocking
- [ ] Tests use proper coroutine testing

### UI Tests
- [ ] **All new screens have UI tests**
- [ ] **All custom components have UI tests**
- [ ] All UI tests pass locally
- [ ] UI tests cover user interactions
- [ ] UI tests cover navigation
- [ ] UI tests cover error states
- [ ] UI tests cover loading states
- [ ] UI tests use semantic matchers
- [ ] Hilt integration tests set up correctly

### Test Execution
- [ ] `./gradlew test` passes
- [ ] `./gradlew connectedAndroidTest` passes
- [ ] No test warnings or errors
- [ ] Code coverage meets minimum thresholds
- [ ] Test report reviewed

## ✅ Documentation

- [ ] Code has KDoc comments for public APIs
- [ ] Complex logic is explained with comments
- [ ] README updated if needed
- [ ] Architecture documentation updated if needed
- [ ] New dependencies documented
- [ ] Breaking changes documented

## ✅ Dependencies

- [ ] No unnecessary dependencies added
- [ ] Dependencies use version catalog (`libs.versions.toml`)
- [ ] Dependencies are latest stable versions
- [ ] Transitive dependencies checked
- [ ] License compatibility verified

## ✅ Performance

- [ ] No performance regressions
- [ ] Large lists use `LazyColumn`/`LazyRow`
- [ ] Images optimized
- [ ] Memory leaks checked
- [ ] No blocking operations on main thread
- [ ] Coroutines used for async operations

## ✅ Security

- [ ] No sensitive data hardcoded
- [ ] No API keys in code
- [ ] Input validation implemented
- [ ] Error messages don't leak sensitive info
- [ ] ProGuard rules updated if needed

## ✅ Accessibility

- [ ] Content descriptions added for icons
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 48dp
- [ ] Text is readable (contrast, size)
- [ ] Screen reader tested
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works

## ✅ Git

- [ ] Commit messages are clear and descriptive
- [ ] Commits are atomic (one logical change)
- [ ] Branch name follows convention
- [ ] No merge conflicts
- [ ] No debug code committed
- [ ] No commented-out code
- [ ] `.gitignore` updated if needed

## ✅ Build

- [ ] Project builds successfully
- [ ] No build warnings
- [ ] ProGuard/R8 rules work (if applicable)
- [ ] APK size is reasonable
- [ ] Min SDK version respected
- [ ] Target SDK version correct

## ✅ Code Review Readiness

- [ ] PR title is clear and descriptive
- [ ] PR description explains what and why
- [ ] Screenshots/videos added for UI changes
- [ ] Related issues linked
- [ ] Breaking changes highlighted
- [ ] Migration guide provided if needed
- [ ] Reviewers assigned
- [ ] Labels added

## ✅ Definition of Done

A feature/bug fix is **ONLY** complete when:
- ✅ All code quality checks pass
- ✅ **All unit tests written and passing**
- ✅ **All UI tests written and passing**
- ✅ Code coverage meets minimum thresholds
- ✅ All documentation updated
- ✅ Code reviewed and approved
- ✅ No merge conflicts
- ✅ CI/CD pipeline passes

## Commands to Run Before PR

```bash
# Format code
./gradlew ktlintFormat

# Run lint
./gradlew lint

# Run unit tests
./gradlew test

# Run instrumented tests
./gradlew connectedAndroidTest

# Generate test coverage
./gradlew jacocoTestReport

# Build release APK
./gradlew assembleRelease
```

## Common Rejection Reasons

Your PR will be **REJECTED** if:
- ❌ Tests are missing
- ❌ Tests are failing
- ❌ Code coverage is below threshold
- ❌ Hardcoded values present
- ❌ Lint errors exist
- ❌ Build fails
- ❌ No responsive design implementation
- ❌ Poor code quality
- ❌ No documentation

## Notes

- Don't skip any items in this checklist
- If an item doesn't apply, explain why in PR description
- When in doubt, ask for clarification
- Quality over speed - take time to do it right